# What the engine's tools, tests and builds write inside it. These hold
# wherever the engine is checked out: the site's engine/ directory, or a
# repository of its own (A10), where the site's rules no longer apply.

# Python and uv: bytecode, an environment made by a bare `uv` against this
# project (a site's own is its .venv, `make venv`), tool caches.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
/.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
# cabal, for a build of the engine on its own.
dist-newstyle/

# Downloaded by tools/download-*.sh and checked against the pins beside
# them; fetched by tools/browser/fetch_axe.py and checked against
# axe-version.
/static/pdfjs/
/static/leaflet/
/static/transformers/
/static/vega/
/static/models/
/tools/browser/axe.min.js

# Written beside static images: WebP companions (tools/convert-images.sh)
# and dimension sidecars (tools/extract-dimensions.py); the golden
# fixture's sidecar is test input (the expected width and height of
# plate.png), and a fresh checkout without it failed the golden test.
/static/**/*.webp
# and the record of which of those the tools made (tools/derived_images.py),
# with what a build makes of it for its pages (build/DerivedImages.hs).
/data/derived-images.json
/data/pairings/
# What those tools leave when a run is stopped: a file being encoded, a
# directory with a file taken aside while its name is given to the new
# one, a record being saved. The next run clears them or puts them back,
# and a site's build asks for a committed engine first (engine.mk
# engine-committed). A file kept for its author (`.previous-image-…`, no
# `.tmp`) is not ignored.
.convert-*/
.thumb-*/
.previous-image-*.tmp/
/data/.derived-images.json.*.tmp
**/*.dims.yaml
!/tests/golden/*.dims.yaml
# The fixture site's are its content, as a site's own would be.
!/fixture-site/**/*.dims.yaml

# Local agent instructions, as in each site.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
